IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s77-84`

-- wra3-sch13.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Schedule 13 (the Social Mobility and Child Poverty
-- Commission). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Host Act (not among the sources): the Child Poverty Act 2010 (CPA). The paragraphs of Schedule 13 are not numbered in the
-- text, so names below cite the CPA section the paragraph amends (CPA 18(1), CPA 18(3)) and not a paragraph number.
-- Only the three definitions that Part 2 gives the amended Act are encoded here. The rest of the Schedule creates, staffs and
-- funds a body and amends other Acts to list it (reason 2, machinery); see NOTES.md, Coverage (wra3).

§ `sch 13 the Commission`

DECLARE `sch 13 body` IS ONE OF
    `sch 13 the Social Mobility and Child Poverty Commission`
    `sch 13 the former Child Poverty Commission`
    `sch 13 any other body`

-- "the Commission": section 8(1) as substituted names "a body called the Social Mobility and Child Poverty Commission (in this
-- Act referred to as 'the Commission')", and section 18(1) is changed so that its definition of "the Commission" has that name.
-- src:3534 | (1) There is to be a body called the Social Mobility and Child Poverty Commission (in this Act referred to as “the Commission”).
@ref sch 13 CPA 8(1) the Commission (src:3534)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `sch 13 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 CPA 8(1) the body is the Commission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `sch 13 the Social Mobility and Child Poverty Commission` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the definition in section 18(1) is not printed, only the substitution of the name in it
    WHEN `sch 13 the former Child Poverty Commission` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say whether any other body is "the Commission"
    WHEN `sch 13 any other body` THEN NOTHING

-- src:3631 | (2) In the definition of “the Commission” in subsection (1), for “Child Poverty Commission” there is substituted “ Social Mobility and Child Poverty Commission ”.
@ref sch 13 CPA 18(1) the Commission (src:3631)
GIVEN `the name in the definition` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`sch 13 CPA 18(1) the name that now stands in the definition of the Commission` MEANS
    -- the substituted name stands in place of "Child Poverty Commission"
    IF `the name in the definition` EQUALS "Child Poverty Commission"
    THEN JUST "Social Mobility and Child Poverty Commission"
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text substitutes for one name only
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `sch 13 Minister of the Crown`

-- "Minister of the Crown" has the same meaning as in the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975, which is not among the sources: the
-- borrowed fact is a plain input, passed through unchanged (NOTHING stays NOTHING).
-- src:3633 | “Minister of the Crown” has the same meaning as in the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975;
@ref sch 13 CPA 18(1) Minister of the Crown (src:3633)
GIVEN `the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975 gives the person that meaning` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 CPA 18(1) the person is a Minister of the Crown` MEANS
    `the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975 gives the person that meaning`

§ `sch 13 appointed day for Northern Ireland`

-- "appointed day for Northern Ireland" means such day as a Minister of the Crown may by order with the consent of the Northern
-- Ireland Assembly appoint (and different days may be appointed for different provisions of the Part). The day appointed for the
-- provision asked about, whether a Minister of the Crown made the order and whether the Assembly consented are plain inputs.
-- src:3635 | (3) In this Part “appointed day for Northern Ireland” means such day as a Minister of the Crown may by order with the consent of the Northern Ireland Assembly appoint (and different days may be appointed for the purposes of different provisions of this Part).
@ref sch 13 CPA 18(3) the appointed day for Northern Ireland (src:3635)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day appointed for the provision by the order` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a Minister of the Crown made the order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order has the consent of the Northern Ireland Assembly` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 13 CPA 18(3) the day is the appointed day for Northern Ireland for the provision` MEANS
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results`
        (LIST
            `a Minister of the Crown made the order`
          , `the order has the consent of the Northern Ireland Assembly`
          , CONSIDER `the day appointed for the provision by the order`
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means such day as a Minister of the Crown may by order ... appoint" (a closed definition: a day other than the one appointed is not it)
            WHEN JUST appointed THEN JUST (appointed EQUALS `the day`)
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no day has been appointed for the provision, so the text gives no day
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        )
